     $person holds a reference to an Account object that I have kept publicly accessible
for the sake of brevity (as you know, I would usually restrict access to a property,
providing an accessor method, if necessary). When the clone is created, it holds a
reference to the same Account object that $person references. I demonstrate this by
adding to the $person object’s Account and confirming the increased balance via
$person2.
     If I do not want an object property to be shared after a clone operation, then it is up
to me to clone it explicitly in the __clone() method:

// listing 04.104
public function __clone(): void
{
    $this->id = 0;
    $this->account = clone $this->account;
}

